From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: PS5: games take the language MihawkOS's setup chose; the shell stays English

The guided setup's language sets the mihawk prefix's Windows locale (docs/GUIDED_SETUP.md): the title pins it in the
prefix when the prefix is made and passes it to every session as WINE_PS5_LOCALE, which helpers inherit
(wine/ps5/pw_wine_inherit.h). Wine reads a process's locale from LC_CTYPE and LC_MESSAGES, which the title cannot give
Explorer and its games apart: a helper's Unix environment is its spawner's. So the language is applied here, in every
process but the session's Explorer, the one the title started with MIHAWK_SESSION=1 in its application environment
(patch 0996), which no program it starts inherits (patch 0998). Games then see the language as their system locale,
user locale and UI language, and Wine's default keyboard layout follows the user locale; the Mihawk OS shell keeps
English. Typed characters still follow the PS5 driver's US key map.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c
@@ -741,6 +741,21 @@
         FIXME_(nls)( "Failed to set LC_CTYPE to %s, is the locale supported?\n", debugstr_a(ctype) );
     if (!(messages = setlocale( LC_MESSAGES, "" )) && (messages = getenv( "LC_MESSAGES" )))
         FIXME_(nls)( "Failed to set LC_MESSAGES to %s, is the locale supported?\n", debugstr_a(messages) );
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* The language MihawkOS's setup chose for this prefix (the title's WINE_PS5_LOCALE, which every helper inherits):
+     * Windows programs take it as their system and user locale, and so their UI language and keyboard layout. The
+     * Mihawk OS shell stays English: its Explorer is the process the title started with MIHAWK_SESSION=1 in its
+     * application environment (patches 0996, 0998), which the programs it starts do not inherit. */
+    {
+        extern const char *pw_ps5_initial_environment(void);
+        const char *language = getenv( "WINE_PS5_LOCALE" ), *item;
+        BOOL shell = FALSE;
+
+        for (item = pw_ps5_initial_environment(); item && *item; item += strlen( item ) + 1)
+            if (!strcmp( item, "MIHAWK_SESSION=1" )) shell = TRUE;
+        if (language && *language && !shell) ctype = messages = language;
+    }
+#endif
 
     if (!unix_to_win_locale( ctype, system_locale )) system_locale[0] = 0;
     TRACE_(nls)( "Unix LC_CTYPE is %s, setting system locale to %s\n", debugstr_a(ctype), debugstr_a(user_locale) );
